Done on the branch — head `98f4d437f9`. The two twins are extracted into one helper in `lib/src/cli/tui_status_line.dart`:

```dart
/// Validates a `tui.*` boolean flag (`classic:`, `showCompactionDetails:`);
/// false when unset. The [key] is the full dotted name — the error names
/// it so a typo'd value points at the right line.
bool _tuiBoolFlag(String key, Object? value) {
  if (value != null && value is! bool) {
    throw ConfigException('"$key" must be a boolean');
  }
  return value as bool? ?? false;
}
```

`parseTuiSection` now calls `_tuiBoolFlag('tui.classic', …)` and `_tuiBoolFlag('tui.showCompactionDetails', …)` — the next `tui.*` boolean reuses it instead of growing a third twin. Error messages are byte-identical to before (both pinned verbatim in `test/cli/tui_status_line_test.dart`: `"tui.classic" must be a boolean`, `"tui.showCompactionDetails" must be a boolean`). `dart test test/cli/tui_status_line_test.dart` — 103 tests passed.
","path":"outputs/review_replies/thread_3.md"}

